\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0    Father, whose everlasting love,
\par \pard\li180\sl202\slmult0\qj  Thy only Son for sinners gave,
\par  Whose grace to all did freely move,
\par  And sent Him down the world to save.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   Help us Thy mercy to extol!
\par \pard\li180\sl202\slmult0  Immense, unfathomed, unconfined;
\par  To praise the Lamb who died for all,
\par  The general Saviour of mankind.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Thy undistinguishing regard
\par \pard\li180\sl202\slmult0  Was cast on Adam's fallen race;
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 For all Thou hast in Christ prepared
\par Sufficient, Sovereign, saving grace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  The world He suffered to redeem;
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 For all He hath the atonement made;
\par For those that will not come to Him,
\par \pard\li144\sl202\slmult0   The ransome of His life was paid.
\par 
\par \pard\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Arise, O God, maintain Thy cause:
\par \pard\li144\sl202\slmult0   The fullness of the Gentiles' call:
\par   Lift up the standard of Thy Cross,
\par  And all shall own Thou diedst for all.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

